{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00451",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 1.0,
      "end_seconds": 3.43,
      "duration_seconds": 2.43,
      "text": "Morning. Just put your bag down anywhere."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 4.44,
      "end_seconds": 5.29,
      "duration_seconds": 0.85,
      "text": "Thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 6.64,
      "end_seconds": 12.79,
      "duration_seconds": 6.15,
      "text": "Hello, um, doctor. I hope it's alright if I stay in for this."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 14.31,
      "end_seconds": 20.62,
      "duration_seconds": 6.31,
      "text": "So, please do. Extra information is always welcome. Sorry about the wait, we're running a bit behind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 22.01,
      "end_seconds": 26.87,
      "duration_seconds": 4.86,
      "text": "Oh, that's fine. I was just reading something on my phone."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 27.41,
      "end_seconds": 30.89,
      "duration_seconds": 3.48,
      "text": "What was the main thing you wanted to talk about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 31.35,
      "end_seconds": 37.25,
      "duration_seconds": 5.9,
      "text": "Well, doctor, it's pain in my right shoulder. It's getting on my nerves now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 38.33,
      "end_seconds": 40.52,
      "duration_seconds": 2.19,
      "text": "How long have you had it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 41.53,
      "end_seconds": 50.43,
      "duration_seconds": 8.9,
      "text": "Hm. It was either the end of last month or earlier than that. I couldn't tell you the date."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 51.79,
      "end_seconds": 57.91,
      "duration_seconds": 6.12,
      "text": "Can you describe it a bit more for me? How strong it is, what the pattern is, what helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 59.43,
      "end_seconds": 93.85,
      "duration_seconds": 34.42,
      "text": "Reaching behind and lifting my arm definitely sets it off. It happens a couple of times a week. I'd rather know what's going on than keep guessing. Oh, and trouble lifting my arm. That's been about the same, about a week. So, I've also had a click in the shoulder. I've had a dull ache down the arm too, um, for about two weeks. As for dull ache down the arm, honestly, a couple of times a week."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 94.5,
      "end_seconds": 98.68,
      "duration_seconds": 4.18,
      "text": "Have you had any chest pain, numbness in the hand or fever?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 99.04,
      "end_seconds": 104.34,
      "duration_seconds": 5.3,
      "text": "No chest pain, numbness in the hand or fever, none of it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 105.78,
      "end_seconds": 107.63,
      "duration_seconds": 1.85,
      "text": "And fall, any of that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 108.81,
      "end_seconds": 111.87,
      "duration_seconds": 3.06,
      "text": "No, I haven't had any fall."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 113.2,
      "end_seconds": 116.01,
      "duration_seconds": 2.81,
      "text": "How about your heart, any problems like that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 117.04,
      "end_seconds": 119.27,
      "duration_seconds": 2.23,
      "text": "Right, no, that's been fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 120.68,
      "end_seconds": 124.55,
      "duration_seconds": 3.87,
      "text": "Do you have everything you need to get home alright?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 125.72,
      "end_seconds": 137.94,
      "duration_seconds": 12.22,
      "text": "Yes, I've got my transport sorted. It's a bit of a trek, but I'm used to the journey by now, and I brought something to read for the wait."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 138.99,
      "end_seconds": 143.36,
      "duration_seconds": 4.37,
      "text": "What about family history, any illnesses that run in the family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 144.59,
      "end_seconds": 150.35,
      "duration_seconds": 5.76,
      "text": "My mother has migraines. Well, you know, my grandmother had breast cancer."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 150.84,
      "end_seconds": 155.88,
      "duration_seconds": 5.04,
      "text": "Are you on any tablets or medication? I ask because it helps me narrow things down."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 157.15,
      "end_seconds": 159.53,
      "duration_seconds": 2.38,
      "text": "It's metformin, twice a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 160.48,
      "end_seconds": 162.31,
      "duration_seconds": 1.83,
      "text": "Do you know the dose?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 163.62,
      "end_seconds": 170.09,
      "duration_seconds": 6.47,
      "text": "It's 500 milligrams. Um, uh, I'm on losartan, 50 milligrams, once a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 171.09,
      "end_seconds": 178.97,
      "duration_seconds": 7.88,
      "text": "Doctor, I think the last prescription for the losartan was 25 milligrams. We changed it at the last visit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 179.87,
      "end_seconds": 182.66,
      "duration_seconds": 2.79,
      "text": "Hm. Do you have the latest prescription with you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 183.7,
      "end_seconds": 187.73,
      "duration_seconds": 4.03,
      "text": "Um, not with me. I'll bring it next time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 188.77,
      "end_seconds": 190.92,
      "duration_seconds": 2.15,
      "text": "Any allergies I should know about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 191.72,
      "end_seconds": 195.6,
      "duration_seconds": 3.88,
      "text": "No, you know, none that I know of."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 197.18,
      "end_seconds": 201.39,
      "duration_seconds": 4.21,
      "text": "What about your general health, any conditions you're being treated for?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 202.78,
      "end_seconds": 214.94,
      "duration_seconds": 12.16,
      "text": "I've, I've had diabetes for five years now. I took the morning off to come in today. Hmm, I've had high blood pressure for nearly five years now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 218.36,
      "end_seconds": 227.56,
      "duration_seconds": 9.2,
      "text": "Mm-hm. Okay, diabetes, that's already on your record. Good to know. Yes, I can see the high blood pressure in your file as well."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 228.26,
      "end_seconds": 230.93,
      "duration_seconds": 2.67,
      "text": "I want to open your previous notes quickly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 231.6,
      "end_seconds": 232.5,
      "duration_seconds": 0.9,
      "text": "Go ahead."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 244.77,
      "end_seconds": 248.36,
      "duration_seconds": 3.59,
      "text": "Alright, I've got it. I'll take a few measurements first."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 259.82,
      "end_seconds": 261.33,
      "duration_seconds": 1.51,
      "text": "Just relax your arm..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 283.13,
      "end_seconds": 302.93,
      "duration_seconds": 19.8,
      "text": "Okay: respiratory rate 15, pressure 119 over 68, oxygen saturation is 97 percent. And pulse 67. Putting together what you've described, it fits best with a rotator cuff problem. I want to be honest that this is an impression, not a final answer. It could also be a pinched nerve in the neck, so we'll keep that open."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 304.04,
      "end_seconds": 307.49,
      "duration_seconds": 3.45,
      "text": "Uh, is this going to go away?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 308.66,
      "end_seconds": 325.07,
      "duration_seconds": 16.41,
      "text": "I can't promise yet, but most people with a rotator cuff problem do well once it's treated properly. Let me just recap so I've got it right. You've had pain in your right shoulder, and no fall or numbness in the hand."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 326.3,
      "end_seconds": 329.35,
      "duration_seconds": 3.05,
      "text": "Exactly, you know, that's what's been happening."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 330.43,
      "end_seconds": 333.92,
      "duration_seconds": 3.49,
      "text": "Do you need me to explain anything as we go?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 334.66,
      "end_seconds": 342.62,
      "duration_seconds": 7.96,
      "text": "Just tell me in plain language, um, please. I'm not good with the medical terms."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 343.27,
      "end_seconds": 350.27,
      "duration_seconds": 7.0,
      "text": "Let's get an ultrasound of the shoulder, for shoulder pain. It's a routine test and it'll give us a much clearer picture."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 351.28,
      "end_seconds": 352.87,
      "duration_seconds": 1.59,
      "text": "Okay, that's fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 354.3,
      "end_seconds": 361.83,
      "duration_seconds": 7.53,
      "text": "I'd like to arrange an X-ray of the shoulder for shoulder pain. The result will help us decide whether anything more is needed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 362.86,
      "end_seconds": 363.79,
      "duration_seconds": 0.93,
      "text": "Okay, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 365.1,
      "end_seconds": 391.37,
      "duration_seconds": 26.27,
      "text": "I'd like you to take naproxen, 250 milligrams, twice a day after food, for five days. That's for shoulder pain. I'll put all of this in writing so you don't have to remember it. Gentle pendulum exercises, I'll show you a couple, but nothing overhead for a bit. Make sure you're drinking plenty of fluids, two to three litres a day if you can, and get proper rest."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 391.73,
      "end_seconds": 402.79,
      "duration_seconds": 11.06,
      "text": "I'd like you to see physiotherapy as well, and I'll write the referral. And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 403.35,
      "end_seconds": 404.64,
      "duration_seconds": 1.29,
      "text": "Okay, I will."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 406.17,
      "end_seconds": 415.98,
      "duration_seconds": 9.81,
      "text": "Keep an eye out, and if the symptoms get worse, call us the same day or go to emergency. Let's review you in four weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 416.93,
      "end_seconds": 420.87,
      "duration_seconds": 3.94,
      "text": "Sure, I'll make the appointment on the way out."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 422.12,
      "end_seconds": 425.87,
      "duration_seconds": 3.75,
      "text": "Okay, summarise it for me, what's the plan from your side?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 426.73,
      "end_seconds": 437.15,
      "duration_seconds": 10.42,
      "text": "So, um, I take the naproxen, 250 milligrams, twice a day after food and come back in four weeks. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 437.66,
      "end_seconds": 440.15,
      "duration_seconds": 2.49,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. Good. Look after yourself."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 441.22,
      "end_seconds": 443.6,
      "duration_seconds": 2.38,
      "text": "I appreciate your time, doctor."
    }
  ]
}